WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.940
Nightshades are huge family of plants

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.060
many of which we eat like potatoes

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:07.189
tomatoes, peppers and eggplants.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.760
Some like tomatillos and ground cherries

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:12.049
have a papery structure that grows

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:13.380
around the fruit.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.440
It forms an air pocket that might

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.340
help the seeds disperse like a little

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.280
life raft.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.500
This family comes from South America

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.940
where its fossil origins

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.220
aren't well known.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.660
Previously it was thought

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.310
that tomatillos and ground cherries

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.380
evolved fairly recently at the time the

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.660
Andes rose. But new fossils that look

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.880
just like those wrapped up fruits were

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.400
recently described by researchers.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.559
These fossils prove that these plants were

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:39.149
around at a much earlier time than

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:41.399
anyone thought, when South America was

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:43.170
still very close to Antarctica

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.030
Australia. And even southern South

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.530
America where the fossils were found was

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.060
warm and wet.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.920
It also means these plants

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.050
evolved not just in South America but

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.629
likely in Antarctica too before it froze over.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.879
Those are totally different

00:00:56.879 --> 00:00:58.949
evolutionary conditions which makes you

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:01.289
wonder what else don't we know about our

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:03.069
favorite foods

